<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Thanks for it all... &nbsp;(Read 456 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=51" title="View the profile of Pepa">Pepa</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Global Moderator<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/stargmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/stargmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/stargmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/stargmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/stargmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 85<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/sephirot.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Evil Druid! (retired)<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=51"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1416.msg14378#msg14378"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/sad.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1416.msg14378#msg14378">Thanks for it all...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> February 08, 2005, 08:05:56 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							After four years, it is time for this druid to find a port outta here! Those four years have been great and hold many memories for me. Although there are way WAY too many to name, there are some that I just can&#039;t go without mentioning....<br /><br />Sindee...my very first guild leader. The days with Shadows of Honor will always have a very special place in my heart.<br />Nokyli...my second guild leader and very dear friend. I pray that God always watch over you and your wife and help you get that garden to grow!<br />Ciil...my mentor and friend. Although you left a long time before I did, you were always the best druid I knew. Thanks for everything!<br />Kweil....(thought I forgot didn&#039;t ya? :P) Even though you beat me to lvl 60, I still won by beating you to 65....and 70! You were always a good friend, and just like Ciil, would come running anytime I needed you. *hugs*<br />Fleak.... 3 was the limit! You always asked, and well, there ya go! (no it&#039;s not dirty for all you gutter-minds, he however, knows what I am talking about!)<br />Kaidog...../smooch miss ya cutie!<br />Kilaer....you and I have known each other for a long time. I am very fortunate to have met such a sweet lady. We do, however, share one memory of a special person we both knew well. God bless Chonan and may he rest in peace.<br />Leithal (Nynne), Kumaddar, Alcoll, Yanke and Debonshire (Lindale)....we got in more trouble together than any 6 people should be allowed. Will cherish those good times forever.<br />Phad....the first person other than Kimmie that I ever met in this game. Thanks for welcoming me to DA with open arms. You were, are and will forever be the nicest person on RN.<br />Thecklos, Beckah....thanks to you two for giving me the chance to be a member of the best officer core on this server. Believe it or not, I enjoyed every min of it no matter how hard it got to be.<br />Tilien....you owe me BBQ! You may not have known it but I looked up to you. You taught me what it meant to be a raiding druid. It was because of you that I switched my spec from Evoc to Alt and I never regretted it!<br />Matteo...The Iron Fist! You spoke, we listened and it was great!<br />Gobbin....the best Necro there is, hands down!<br />Chubz...I never, EVER &quot;let&quot; you die! If you were tanking, I was healing. Don&#039;t let anyone get ya down hun, you are one of the best tanks DA could ever have. Keep up with that school work though, it will get you much farther than this game ever will!<br />Feilynn...Such a good friend you turned out to be. Keep in touch hun, you and your family will always be in my prayers and on my mind. That mess over there has to end eventually, right? *hugs*<br />The rest of Dol Amroth.....You guys are great! The best guild on RN hands down. I will never forget the great times on raids and in grinds. I will miss you all!!<br />Echoes In Eternity.... I know some, if not most of you don&#039;t like me, I still thought of ALL of you (yes even Jeet!) as the perfect match for us to ally with. I would never have enjoyed EQ as much the last year if all you guys hadn&#039;t been a part of it. May you continue to break new ground in the land of Norrath. I will miss you all!<br /><br />If I didn&#039;t mention you, don&#039;t be upset. It&#039;s hard to remember everyone that had an impact on my EQ life when I am looking through tears. I know a long drawn out goodbye like this seems stupid to some people but to those that log on and wonder where I have been, this is my answer. EQ took up four long years of my life and those are years of my kids life I can never get back. I am hoping laying this game to rest will somehow mend the wounds I caused in that department. I do play WoW when time permits. I can log on there for a couple of hours and get a whole lot done without sacrificing my family to do it. If you are playing that on Illdan, Horde side, look me up. Pepa, my Undead priest or Amah my Tauren druid, still learning and still lowbie but having a good time.<br /><br /><br />HUGS to all of Rodcet Nife! Have a wonderful time in the land of Norrath!<br />*The hardest thing I have ever had to do was hit the &quot;Post&quot; button*
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><br /><img src="http://home.earthlink.net/~pepa_stormshyld/Pepa-1.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br /><a href="http://www.battlezinc.com/dolamroth" target="_blank"><span style="color: purple;"><b>DA Home Page</b></span></a><br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=298411" target="_blank"><span style="color: purple;"><b>Inspect Me!</b></span></a></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg14379"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=79" title="View the profile of Griglon">Griglon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 8<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://home.sc.rr.com/mppandclp/images/grig_face.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=79"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1416.msg14379#msg14379"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1416.msg14379#msg14379">Re: Thanks for it all...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> February 08, 2005, 09:19:30 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Going to miss you Hon!  <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/missyou.gif" alt="missyou" border="0" />  Take good care of yourself and don&#039;t be a stranger on the email!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
